1
00:00:07,470 --> 00:00:08,480
Enemies?

2
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,190
What nation's battleship is that?

3
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:13,770
It probably belongs to 
the Bloodchain Brigade.

4
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:16,320
What? The Bloodchain Brigade?

5
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:22,510
So the rats scurried right into the trap?

6
00:00:22,510 --> 00:00:23,370
Rats?

7
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:27,000
The Bloodchain Brigade are the most 
extreme of the anti-Highlander factions.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,890
They've been getting out of hand, 
and it's become a problem.

9
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:34,580
So I set a trap.

10
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:37,940
You knew about the Bloodchain Brigade?

11
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:39,420
Obviously.

12
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:41,040
A trap, you say?

13
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,800
Nothing complicated.

14
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,410
We just set up a fake ceremony.

15
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:50,530
Then I, an Arch Lord, attended.

16
00:00:50,530 --> 00:00:52,420
A fake ceremony?

17
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:56,280
Then the new Hyral Menas...?

18
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,560
That was a lie, of course.

19
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:02,860
Our goal was to lure the rats out 
into the open and exterminate them.

20
00:01:03,210 --> 00:01:06,090
So we were just pawns, then?

21
00:01:06,090 --> 00:01:09,290
Then why did His Majesty 
have to face such humiliation?

22
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:14,390
None of you have meaning! 
None of you have value!

23
00:01:14,390 --> 00:01:18,170
You're all worthless, helpless trash that 
can't do anything but crawl on the ground!

24
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:19,460
That's so cruel!

25
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:23,890
Wonderful!

26
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:29,080
So what you're saying 
is that you're a bad guy

27
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,100
who not only lied to our king, 
but also cut off his arm.

28
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:35,100
I've got that right, don't I?

29
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:39,080
Yup. I commend you for your excellent 
understanding of the situation.

30
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:45,230
Your Majesty, order me to strike 
this criminal down, and I will.

31
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:47,650
You must not kill him.

32
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:48,880
Capture him alive.

33
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:50,590
As you wish.

34
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:52,560
You heard the man.

35
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:56,300
So the situation has changed. 
I'll be taking you up on that duel.

36
00:01:56,530 --> 00:02:00,010
Sure, but I've got other 
people to fight today.

37
00:02:00,010 --> 00:02:01,760
Let's make it quick.

38
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,420
Give me all you've got!

39
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:05,140
Thank you!

40
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:10,290
<i>Is that pale light... magic?</i>

41
00:02:10,290 --> 00:02:13,190
<i>No, it's nothing I've ever sensed before.</i>

42
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:17,160
<i>This woman's a threat 
like none I've ever seen...</i>

43
00:02:17,490 --> 00:02:18,150
<i>So I'll...</i>

44
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:25,570
<i>Come on. The second you touch this wall, 
you'll lose an arm or a leg,</i>

45
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,420
<i>just like that knight and your king did!</i>

46
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:31,080
What's wrong?

47
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,660
Come and get me.

48
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:38,720
That magic, it's an "annihilation" effect 
that destroys whatever touches it, right?

49
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,280
<i>How did she know?</i>

50
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:44,560
<i>Can she see this wall?</i>

51
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:50,300
It looks like surrounding your whole body 
with it weakened the effects.

52
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:54,780
It'd be stronger if you concentrated 
your power in one spot.

53
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:58,530
Go ahead and do that, please.

54
00:02:58,530 --> 00:03:00,750
I'll attack that point.

55
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:05,030
Are you stupid?

56
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:10,520
If I do that, and you just attack 
a different spot, I'm finished!

57
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:13,810
If I wanted to do that, 
I'd already have attacked you.

58
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:16,880
You can't believe me?

59
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:22,840
For a Highlander Arch Lord, 
you're kind of a coward.

60
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:28,980
Nice!

61
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,440
Chris!

62
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:34,400
Come on! I'll just pray you're not a liar!

63
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:36,620
Of course! Here I go!

64
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:43,800
<i>If I use an aether-imbued attack 
to destroy the magic structure itself...</i>

65
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:55,130
Oops!

66
00:03:55,490 --> 00:03:57,220
Where do you think he fell?

67
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:59,840
Well, that's Chris for you...

68
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:18,060
<u>Reborn</u>

69
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:18,060
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

70
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:18,060
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

71
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:35,430
Episode 11      Butt-Kicking Squire

72
00:05:41,330 --> 00:05:48,200
We have no choice now but to 
destroy the Bloodchain Brigade!

73
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:52,900
We may be able to use that to restore 
relations with the Highland.

74
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:53,900
Go!

75
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:54,920
Yes, Your Majesty!

76
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:57,050
Sire, please evacuate.

77
00:05:57,050 --> 00:05:59,610
Everyone but His Majesty's guards, 
go on the attack!

78
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:01,190
Yes, sir!

79
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:04,960
We'll go engage the Bloodchain Brigade, then.

80
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,140
"We"?

81
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:11,170
Chris, I'm a little tired after 
healing His Majesty's arm...

82
00:06:11,650 --> 00:06:14,440
If you want to rest, you can rest near me.

83
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:18,450
Wherever you are is bound to be 
where the fighting's fiercest!

84
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:22,410
It's fine! Come on, come on!

85
00:06:22,410 --> 00:06:25,610
Fine! Fine! Well...

86
00:06:25,610 --> 00:06:28,140
I'll be back later!

87
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:31,350
She seems like someone I can count on.

88
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:36,840
Over there!

89
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:38,660
A Flying Gear!

90
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:40,540
No time for that!

91
00:06:41,490 --> 00:06:44,100
Sorry to bother you!

92
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,670
Wh-What the heck?!

93
00:06:45,670 --> 00:06:47,230
What <i>is</i> that?

94
00:06:47,230 --> 00:06:49,720
A maid! It's an airborne maid!

95
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,380
She's fast!

96
00:06:54,350 --> 00:06:55,770
There we go.

97
00:06:55,770 --> 00:06:59,440
Look, Rani. We're almost at the 
Bloodchain Brigade's battleship.

98
00:06:59,750 --> 00:07:01,630
I knew it'd be the front line...

99
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:08,820
We need to stop them now, 
before they hurt more innocents.

100
00:07:09,170 --> 00:07:11,100
Here we go, Chris!

101
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:14,070
Oh, you're all ready to fight now, huh, Rani?

102
00:07:14,070 --> 00:07:15,830
After seeing that, yeah.

103
00:07:16,230 --> 00:07:18,540
I'll interrupt their attack.

104
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:20,000
What are you going to do?

105
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,970
Go!

106
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,960
Burst!

107
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:25,620
Circle the ship!

108
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:28,530
I see. You're blinding them.

109
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:33,430
I'll stop their attacks. You stop the ship!

110
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:35,310
Okay, got it!

111
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:51,270
Aether Strike!

112
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,390
They deflected it?!

113
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:08,470
<i>I knew it...</i>

114
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:12,800
<i>Leon and Sistia don't seem to be there.</i>

115
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,860
That little girl did that?

116
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:16,760
How can a maid be that powerful?

117
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:18,940
Welcome.

118
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:21,730
I'll be serving you this evening.

119
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,930
That was just my way of welcoming you.

120
00:08:24,930 --> 00:08:27,180
S-Serving us?

121
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,620
Be careful.

122
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:33,400
The more beautiful the rose, the sharper 
its thorns and deadlier its poison.

123
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:37,630
Continue the mission. I'll deal with her.

124
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:47,490
What about your plan 
to save the Hyral Menas?

125
00:08:48,170 --> 00:08:52,700
The principal and my friends 
from the academy are handling it.

126
00:08:53,310 --> 00:08:58,410
And if we don't do anything, 
they might think we're with you.

127
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:03,920
So the two of us came to protect 
the king and the Highlander emissary.

128
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:11,160
Doesn't splitting your forces make it
more likely that you'll fail on both fronts?

129
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:15,410
If I take care of things here 
and get over there before they finish,

130
00:09:15,410 --> 00:09:16,870
I get to have twice the fun!

131
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,840
How bold.

132
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:24,580
While you're being bold, why don't you 
tell me where the Highlander emissary is?

133
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:27,280
Oh, sorry...

134
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,020
I actually don't know.

135
00:09:31,430 --> 00:09:33,460
That's a shame.

136
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:36,930
It appears you've grown stronger than before.

137
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:40,160
I didn't have a way 
of determining that for myself.

138
00:09:40,910 --> 00:09:43,350
But you seem like the perfect opportunity!

139
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:46,250
So you're using me as a way 
to test yourself?

140
00:09:46,990 --> 00:09:49,070
Thanks in advance!

141
00:09:49,070 --> 00:09:50,910
I guess I have no choice, then.

142
00:09:59,610 --> 00:10:02,110
It seems something did happen at the castle!

143
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:09,120
All the troops that were escorting Ripple 
headed back to the castle.

144
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,350
Now is our chance.

145
00:10:10,350 --> 00:10:11,820
Okay.

146
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:17,130
Everyone, I'll say this again: you're under no 
obligation to participate in this operation.

147
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:20,310
Please don't feel like you have to.

148
00:10:20,310 --> 00:10:22,940
Who's going to go home
after being told <i>that</i>?

149
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:25,340
Nobody here is going home.

150
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:28,940
Actually, in that case, 
I'm gonna go home and sleep.

151
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:32,740
Wait! Wait, Yua!

152
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:35,450
We need you here!

153
00:10:35,450 --> 00:10:38,120
You just said I didn't have to do it.

154
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:42,440
We need your help. 
Please lend us your aid.

155
00:10:42,730 --> 00:10:44,960
Mr. Glasses, do you have a fever?

156
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:45,750
No!

157
00:10:45,750 --> 00:10:46,970
I'm just fine!

158
00:10:46,970 --> 00:10:49,350
Oh, you're right. You get mad so fast.

159
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:51,360
Depending on who I'm talking to!

160
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:55,580
This isn't the time! 
We're about to start the mission!

161
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:57,420
I'm asking you to stay, too.

162
00:10:58,070 --> 00:10:59,980
I could really use you on my side.

163
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,720
Ripple...

164
00:11:03,130 --> 00:11:08,180
I thought I had no choice but to accept 
what was happening to me.

165
00:11:09,370 --> 00:11:13,940
A Hyral Menas who can't protect anyone... 
is no Hyral Menas at all.

166
00:11:14,610 --> 00:11:20,520
But you're all doing your absolute best 
to protect me, right?

167
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:24,660
Well, one of you seems 
to just be having fun.

168
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:28,120
True. I won't say who, though.

169
00:11:28,570 --> 00:11:30,940
She's probably sneezing right now.

170
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:33,220
I'm sure she is.

171
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:45,490
The home where I was born 
was destroyed years and years ago.

172
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:50,800
But now this country is my home. 
I can really feel that now.

173
00:11:51,330 --> 00:11:53,380
I understand how I really feel...

174
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:56,090
I know I'm causing trouble for you all,

175
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:58,360
but I want to stay here with 
the people of this country.

176
00:11:59,110 --> 00:12:04,450
So... it's only natural that 
I'd ask for help, right?

177
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:06,070
Ripple...

178
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,620
So, Yua...

179
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:11,050
Yua, Ripple is begging for your help—

180
00:12:11,050 --> 00:12:12,780
Zzz...

181
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:14,530
Hey!

182
00:12:15,030 --> 00:12:16,480
He's interrupting my sleep!

183
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,490
Save me, Lady Animal Ears!

184
00:12:18,490 --> 00:12:22,100
Anyway, I want your help.

185
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:25,480
If it works out, I'll buy you dinner, okay?

186
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:30,170
I don't want food. I want you to 
introduce me to somebody.

187
00:12:32,330 --> 00:12:34,170
What kind of person?

188
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,630
Somebody as cool as Mr. Glasses.

189
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:40,850
Wh-What? It's too late for you to try 
and get on my good side—

190
00:12:40,850 --> 00:12:46,080
Somebody who's not as short-tempered 
or weak as Mr. Glasses...

191
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,830
Why, you...

192
00:12:48,150 --> 00:12:53,500
Okay, now that we've made it to the 
punchline, I'd like to start the mission!

193
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:56,050
The <i>punchline</i>? Ma'am...

194
00:12:56,050 --> 00:12:58,590
Go ahead, Leone.

195
00:12:58,590 --> 00:12:59,400
Okay!

196
00:13:07,030 --> 00:13:12,840
Principal Miliera and I will have Ripple 
absorb our power and summon magicite beasts.

197
00:13:13,310 --> 00:13:16,630
You take them out when they show up!

198
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,980
It's in your hands, everyone.

199
00:13:34,810 --> 00:13:37,910
Spread out in a circle around Ripple!

200
00:13:53,230 --> 00:13:54,170
Here they come!

201
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:07,560
<i>Such incredible power!</i>

202
00:14:08,210 --> 00:14:11,740
<i>I can see why you're the leader 
of the Bloodchain Brigade!</i>

203
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:17,250
Chris, I believe in you!

204
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:29,510
Sorry. I'm not done yet.

205
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,580
That's more than fine by me!

206
00:14:33,110 --> 00:14:38,180
<i>I can sense one more aether flow, 
besides his Aether Shell.</i>

207
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,220
An aether sword?

208
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:47,690
I'm amazed you dodged that. Impressive.

209
00:14:47,690 --> 00:14:52,410
That sword's made of compressed 
and stabilized aether, isn't it?

210
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:56,740
<i>I can use magic to create a sword too, but...</i>

211
00:14:58,740 --> 00:15:05,360
<i>Wielding a compressed aether sword and 
aether armor simultaneously is no mean feat.</i>

212
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:08,020
<i>I can't do that myself yet.</i>

213
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:09,730
It is as you say.

214
00:15:09,730 --> 00:15:11,060
Sorry, but you're mine!

215
00:15:17,210 --> 00:15:19,380
<i>At this distance, he has the advantage.</i>

216
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:21,960
<i>I need to get closer!</i>

217
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,310
<i>But that sword...</i>

218
00:15:23,690 --> 00:15:29,700
<i>If I take a hit from that, even with my 
Aether Shell, I won't be getting off lightly.</i>

219
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:31,570
<i>Which means...</i>

220
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:33,370
<i>I've got one chance!</i>

221
00:15:35,470 --> 00:15:38,570
That weak blade can't stop me!

222
00:15:38,570 --> 00:15:40,540
It doesn't need to!

223
00:15:41,130 --> 00:15:44,200
<i>If it can halt him for even 
a second, I can get close!</i>

224
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:51,590
Aether Strike!

225
00:15:58,450 --> 00:16:01,300
She's approaching the point 
where even I can't stop her?

226
00:16:01,930 --> 00:16:07,520
It sounds like you've been busy. 
But I've been focusing on training.

227
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:10,510
Chris, something's coming! Focus!

228
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:17,040
Ivel! I'm so glad you're okay!

229
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:21,280
What? You were the one who 
kicked me into the sky!

230
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:26,060
Arch Lord... You're the emissary this time?

231
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:29,330
So you're the leader 
of the Bloodchain Brigade?

232
00:16:29,330 --> 00:16:31,250
What a stupid-looking costume.

233
00:16:31,250 --> 00:16:36,400
Get back, Ivel. He's after your life.

234
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:38,530
That's exactly what I want!

235
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:42,850
I'm going to crush their leader, 
before moving on to the rest of the maggots!

236
00:16:42,850 --> 00:16:47,060
Then I suppose I'll need to defend myself.

237
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:51,410
Wait! That's no reason to fight each other!

238
00:16:51,410 --> 00:16:53,040
Why can't we all just get along?

239
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:54,790
You're one to talk!

240
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:59,140
Of course, if you'd both like to fight me...

241
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,030
I've secured the bridge.

242
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:03,700
Well done, Sistia.

243
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:06,300
Things have become rather complicated.

244
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:10,620
Sistia, lend me your strength.

245
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:11,990
With pleasure.

246
00:17:13,350 --> 00:17:17,960
My power, my being... Use them as you like.

247
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:20,810
I entrust it all to you.

248
00:17:21,410 --> 00:17:23,370
The Hyral Menas is becoming a weapon?

249
00:17:23,370 --> 00:17:24,640
Not if I can help it!

250
00:17:38,910 --> 00:17:40,470
Amazing!

251
00:17:41,470 --> 00:17:46,070
<i>It's absorbing aether, 
rather than mana, and amplifying it!</i>

252
00:17:46,490 --> 00:17:49,980
<i>The Hyral Menas lives up to their reputation!</i>

253
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,470
Gotcha.

254
00:17:58,350 --> 00:18:02,130
You really are amazing, Yua.

255
00:18:02,130 --> 00:18:04,050
Thank you, Curly Hair.

256
00:18:04,050 --> 00:18:06,280
But I'm a little tired...

257
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:09,340
I think we're at our limits.

258
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:24,200
Leone...

259
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,490
Thank you!

260
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:31,160
Nice, Two.

261
00:18:31,530 --> 00:18:35,370
She's using her spatial isolation Gift 
at the same time... Well done.

262
00:18:35,370 --> 00:18:38,540
Thank you.

263
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:43,170
But... sorry. I think I'm at my limit...

264
00:18:48,050 --> 00:18:50,180
Is this all we can do?

265
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:53,060
Let's defeat the magicite beasts 
in front of us, at least!

266
00:18:58,320 --> 00:18:59,240
No!

267
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:04,410
Lightning beasts? Is that...

268
00:19:08,650 --> 00:19:10,100
Brother?

269
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:11,710
Hey.

270
00:19:11,710 --> 00:19:15,540
So, um... I'm sure you have a lot 
you want to say to me.

271
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:18,010
But I'm going to help you.

272
00:19:19,650 --> 00:19:22,390
Hey, don't look so mad.

273
00:19:22,390 --> 00:19:25,710
You saw that, right? I'm here to help.

274
00:19:26,090 --> 00:19:29,970
Do you know how much Leone has suffered?

275
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:34,150
Do you think you can atone 
by helping us here?

276
00:19:34,150 --> 00:19:36,320
I understand.

277
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,600
Here.

278
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,960
What is that?

279
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,500
Mana mist.

280
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:46,350
It should help you.

281
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:50,450
He's right... My body feels so light...

282
00:19:51,170 --> 00:19:53,410
That's a big help!

283
00:19:53,410 --> 00:19:57,210
Yeah, my new boss has a lot 
of helpful stuff.

284
00:19:57,210 --> 00:20:00,650
He's the one who told me 
to come here, actually.

285
00:20:02,380 --> 00:20:05,700
You shouldn't keep your desire for justice 
bottled up within you.

286
00:20:06,450 --> 00:20:10,150
If there's something you want 
to protect, go protect it.

287
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:13,560
So I didn't have a choice. No choice at all.

288
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,770
"No choice"?

289
00:20:16,230 --> 00:20:19,050
Leone, seal us all in pocket space again.

290
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:22,430
You're still doubting me?

291
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:24,520
I'm not going to try and trick you.

292
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,190
I-I know!

293
00:20:26,710 --> 00:20:32,000
You're actually a little glad 
I'm here, aren't you?

294
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:34,250
I am not!

295
00:20:44,330 --> 00:20:46,900
You're feeding mana to Ripple, right?

296
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:51,520
Silva...

297
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,300
Right.

298
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:55,020
Get ready, everybody.

299
00:21:26,010 --> 00:21:27,760
Chris! Look!

300
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:30,040
It's from the direction of the academy.

301
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:42,310
Hey, you okay?

302
00:21:42,310 --> 00:21:45,040
Brother, what was that?

303
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,460
Look.

304
00:21:54,460 --> 00:21:58,430
Ripple summoned something unbelievable.

305
00:22:04,290 --> 00:22:07,090
That's... a Prismer!

306
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:50,980
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

307
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:50,980
Don't you wish
 we could've
 worn cute
 outfits too?

308
